Optimization Objectives

The optimization process simultaneously considers two major objectives.

1. Real Power Loss Minimization

The objective is to reduce electrical losses occurring in distribution lines.

Benefits include:

Improved system efficiency
Reduced energy wastage
Lower operating cost
Better utilization of electrical infrastructure

2. Voltage Profile Improvement

The voltage at each bus should remain close to the nominal value.

Benefits include:

Improved power quality
Enhanced voltage stability
Better equipment performance
Increased system reliability

Both objectives are combined using a weighted multi-objective optimization function while satisfying all operational constraints.
